WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- Tell me about Philly.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.960
Were you a cheesesteak guy growing up?

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:03.930
- Oh, I'm a cheesesteak guy.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.340
- Oh, okay.
- Still. Yeah, still.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.370
Well, not right now on the Whole30,

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.600
but you know-
- Okay.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.600
- In Philly, anybody who goes to Philly,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.700
you have to figure out

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.200
which cheesesteak you love.
- Right.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.570
- Do you like Gino's? Do you like Pat's?

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.403
- Gino's and Pat's

00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:16.359
You know, I-
- Have you experienced them?

00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:17.468
- I'm an independent.
- Yeah.

00:00:17.468 --> 00:00:19.790
- I can go either way-
- Either way.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.010
- Depending on the particular steak.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:22.843
- But I have to ask you,

00:00:22.843 --> 00:00:24.950
do you like Cheez Whiz on yours?

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.700
- I opt for the Provolone.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.690
But that's-
- Oh, look at!

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.530
See, this is a man who
really knows cheesesteaks.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.560
- See that is my Italian heritage.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.246
Cheez Whiz, just the
name Whiz turns me off.

00:00:34.246 --> 00:00:36.196
(Colman laughing)

00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:38.250
I don't want any Whiz on my,

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.083
you know, when people say-
- You don't have

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.980
any Whiz on your cheesesteak.
- Yeah, what do you want?

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.854
First time I had one, "Hey,
you want some Whiz on that?"

00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:43.687
No!
(Colman laughing)

00:00:43.687 --> 00:00:46.040
No, I don't want Whiz on it!
- You're like,

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.714
dude, it's just craft.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.547
- It's just craft.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:51.070
- I know, but Whiz-
- Fried onions?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.420
- And it even comes out of a can.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.810
Cheese in a can, yeah, no.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:54.930
So to me, the Provolone,

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.930
the guy cuts and puts
a nice piece on there.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.010
- But do you like it
to look neat or sloppy?

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.910
Because Philly, it's gotta be a mess

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.110
and it's just like, it's
gonna get all over you.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.624
- Yeah, either way is fine.
- Okay, cool.

00:01:03.624 --> 00:01:05.180
- I can, you know, I can-
- I'm not judging.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.322
- I'm not Orthodox, I'm
reformed cheesesteak.

00:01:07.322 --> 00:01:08.155
(Colman laughing)

00:01:08.155 --> 00:01:10.800
So I could go sloppy, yeah, yeah.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.490
Orthodox would be the, yeah,

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.075
but the reformed cheesesteak, yeah, yeah.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.643
(Colman laughing)
It is very good.

